From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:26:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 023/207] deepseek: bound CUDA weight and persistent-form
 upload stages

Whole checkpoint images can exceed the CUDA source-custody budget during
real-pack boot. Copy through a reusable 64 MiB stage instead of reserving
the entire image, keeping device allocations and paired scale addresses
contiguous and preserving full-image metadata and digests.

Wait before each stage reuse and retain the existing poison, drain and
retryable-close contracts when a later chunk fails. Cover exact bytes,
destination offsets, paired ownership and failed-copy custody with the
fake driver. Honor offsets in its small-copy memory model as well.

Credit Jay Leaton's published flash17 recipe for the real-pack reproducer.
